Z||000008||Fformula88||12-28-2001||11:49 AM||||The Saturn Vue's front end isn't all that attractive, but otherwise the vehicle isn't that bad.  I stopped by the Saturn dealer to take a closer look... didn't drive it but wanted to get a close look.  Its not bad in person, nicely proportioned.  However, the interior looks like the typical Saturn cheapo-plastic interiors found in their other cars.  For an all new model I expected it to look a little nicer inside and not so low-budget.  The Jeep Liberty in the same price range looks like a much more expensive vehicle inside.<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/formulasig.JPG">           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">    <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000009||Tigger||12-29-2001||12:50 AM||||I put a VUE through the paces last week.  4 cylinder, 5 speed manual.  It was pretty cool, I was suprise I could burn the tires catching 2nd!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><P>Beats the Aztek hands down for looks.  I'll agree the interior has the GM plastiky look.  I like that it also has the traditional plastic body panels we're all very much familar with.||||reg||14
